{title: His Mercy Endures}
{subtitle: Psalms 106:1}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Ab] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Hallelujah sing to the Lord
[Bb/D]Give thanks for his good[Cm7]ness
His love does not [Ab]fail
[Bb]His mercy endures for[Eb]ever
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Who can re[Cm7]count his mighty [Bb]deeds
Or make [Ab]all his praise be [Eb]heard
Blessed are [Cm7]those who keep justice
[Bb]Doing what is right at all [Eb]times
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Remember me [Bb]Lord when you [Cm7]show favor
Come to me [Ab]with your sal[Eb]vation
Hallelu[Bb]jah for he is [Cm7]good
His [Ab]mercy en[Bb]dures forev[Eb]er [Bb/D][Cm7][Ab]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Give [Eb]thanks to the Lord for he is [Bb/D]good
His mercy en[Cm7]dures forever
Who can re[Ab]count the mighty [Bb]deeds
Or make [Ab]all his praise be [Eb]heard
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
